  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Chlorine pentafluoride is an inter halogen compound.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is colourless liquid. The central chlorine atom is having five bond pairs and one lone pair on it. Hence, according to VSEPR theory it has square pyramidal geometry. It is toxic by inhalation and an irritant to skin, eyes and mucus membranes.</p>"
